  "details": "It would be nice to have a way to move the avatar view on more than the Y axis and to be able to include rotation instead of just position in the temporary pose space state behavior. This would let you create many more unique poses and situations for the player to be in, and grants a lot more freedom to creators to come up with various posing and movement systems.\n\nOf course each axis of translation and rotation could be locked like in rotation constraints, and by default it would replicate the behavior of the current temporary pose space in order to keep current avatars from breaking.",
